BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sex\, Death\, and Kink
DTSTART:20260714T190000
DTEND:20260714T190000
UID:09d1c7ac69d390677618808f305dfe02@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Queer Death Salon is a virtual community space for all 2SLGBTQ
 IA+ people to come together to discuss death\, dying and grief. It is a fa
 cilitated drop-in discussion space\, with the purpose of building connecti
 on\, skill\, and resources for 2SLGBTQIA+ people navigating end of life in
  our personal lives and in our communities. Join Badly Licked Bear for a d
 eep conversation about the ways that sex and death are woven together in f
 etish\, kink and BDSM\, seen through and with a critical eye towards the r
 ealities and illusions of the &quot\;kink escalator\,&quot\; which like th
 e &quot\;relationship escalator\,&quot\; both suggests and expects illusio
 ns of &quot\;progress&quot\; as a goal\, while also looking at the advanta
 ges of living and playing and loving in both the deep and the shallow ends
  of the pool. Badly Licked Bear is an educator\, storyteller\, artist\, an
 d mutual aid worker. A former curator and college professor\, she teaches\
 , speaks\, and writes at the intersections of film\, culture\, politics an
 d sexuality. She also works as a voice and activist for transgender civil 
 rights and practical\, transformative sexuality in the BDSM\, kink\, and l
 eather communities. ‍
LOCATION:Online\, online
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/sex-death-and-kink
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sapphic Literary Social
DTSTART:20260714T190000
DTEND:20260714T190000
UID:480aa8d65120834f53a8c236126398b7@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:we invite you to a sapphic reading social! 📖when: Tuesday J
 uly 14\, 2026 📔where: @bampothouse of tea! 📖what to bring: a gently-
 used book\, wrapped either at home or on-site at our wrapping station 📔
 tickets are PWYC at the link in bio 📖when you arrive with your wrapped 
 book\, you’ll be given a label and asked to write a description of the b
 ook’s themes without spoiling the title. Then\, the books will be placed
  on a shelf and readers will have the chance to peruse the selection. For 
 the first hour\, guests will settle in\, order iced tea\, cocktails\, or f
 ood\, and talk about queer literature using curated conversation prompts. 
 We also invite you to decorate and design your own bookmarks. As the event
  progresses\, we’ll announce the winners of bookish giveaways from vendo
 rs like @anotherstorybookshop !!! Around 8:30\, the book exchange will tak
 e place :) ‍
LOCATION:Bampot\, 201 Harbord St
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/sapphic-literary-social
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
